KZ3 patch 1066 (SPU pass 49): cellSpursJoinTaskset returned at once, so a taskset re-created at the same address
right after Shutdown + Join (KZ3's Bink: two tasksets at fixed EAs, re-created at every movie switch) had its old
task (same taskset EA, same task id) still alive on its host thread next to the new one. Both park in WAIT_SIGNAL on
the same SIGNALLED bit; the old one could consume the new task's first signal, the new task waited forever and the
PPU's Bink wait loop (0xCB8424, usleep(400) at lr 0xCB8594) never ended (the intermittent menu-movie stall). The old
task's exit also cleared the new task's ready/pending/enabled bits and its running mark. Now each task thread
remembers the taskset generation it started in; Join waits (bounded, KZ3_JOIN_TASKSET_MS, default 1000) for the
taskset's running, not parked, tasks to finish, then bumps the generation; a parked task of an older generation never
consumes a signal again and its exit leaves the new tasks' state alone. KZ3_JOIN_TASKSET_OLD=1 = the old behaviour.
One "[ts-join]" line per join (first 32, then every 64th, and every timeout). Upstream candidate (general).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): upstream's coherent signal watch + 1066's parked count; 1067's `!cut` on upstream's moved signalled update.

